- op: discuss  # 95ae
  at: '2026-10-28T14:46:07Z'  # 95ae
  by: agent  # 95ae
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 95ae
  clock: 6  # 95ae
  nonce: 95ae  # 95ae
  message: "2026-10-28: implemented on an uncommitted branch and MEASURED as pre-registered; NOT shipped, because this item says the owner rules on the delta. Rows: argv (python sys.argv + argparse parse_args/parse_known_args, js/ts process.argv, rust std::env::args/args_os, elixir System.argv, haskell getArgs, erlang init:get_argument*, swift CommandLine.arguments) declared env_read AND ipc_recv, simultaneous; document.cookie declared browser_storage_read (the medium) AND env_read, simultaneous. Patch: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/zidam_10282026/zidam.patch; plan PLAN.md, results RESULTS.md beside it. DELTA (10 repos x 7 generic claims): only the two untrusted_input claims move; no host_secret verdict changes (the cookie move keeps its label). 6 verdicts flip inconclusive -> violated (arti subprocess; growthbook host-fs + subprocess; jaeger host-fs; livebook host-fs + subprocess); counts grow elsewhere, e.g. qemu-meson host-fs 99 -> 351 and subprocess 83 -> 173, sherpa-onnx host-fs 1 -> 56. Seeded sample of 10 new argv rows: 10/10 correct or plausible, 0/10 useful -- each is a CLI or script doing with its own arguments what it exists to do (4 are qemu-meson 'test cases/' fixtures the production scope did not exclude). OPTIONS FOR THE OWNER: (a) ship as is; (b) ship with argv's untrusted_input rows marked so a claim can set them aside (a disclosed exclusion like resource_naming_only); (c) keep argv host_secret-only and record the ruling's measured cost. Also open: the scalar primary io_boundary of the simultaneous cookie / INV-dadu URL rows follows registry order (env_read first), not the medium; consumers read the full list since WI-votat."  # 95ae
