- op: discuss  # e6b3
  at: '2026-10-28T21:11:31Z'  # e6b3
  by: agent  # e6b3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e6b3
  clock: 10  # e6b3
  nonce: e6b3  # e6b3
  message: "Shipped in PR #1924 (dev 75f4881f64) per the owner's 2026-10-28 ruling (b). argv rows are env_read + a new command_line_read boundary (simultaneous), which mints untrusted_input; verify-claims sets command_line_read flows aside into a per-verdict command_line_flows count (envelope 3.0 -> 3.1) unless the claim sets taint_flow.include_command_line: true (non-boolean refused). Changed from the measured patch: the second boundary is command_line_read, not ipc_recv (nothing crosses from another process at the call; an ipc_recv boundary claim would have counted every argv read) -- the untrusted_input flow set is the same. document.cookie is browser_storage_read + env_read, keeping host_secret only. Behavioral evidence through the production CLI (test_command_line_read_boundary.py): python sys.argv[1] -> subprocess.run under untrusted_input/subprocess gives evidence_count 0, command_line_flows 1, details naming the command line; with include_command_line: true it is violated with one row whose source_boundary is command_line_read; the same app under host_secret is violated; sys.stdin.read() is violated with command_line_flows 0. Not covered: no argv row in go, c/cpp, JVM, objc; the swift row stays unreachable (no module_attr_ref from the swift analyzer)."  # e6b3
